  "id": "COMPOUND:21963 - PROTEIN:4740",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but coherent pathway linking Lambertiainc Acid to the Serine/threonine-protein kinase pim-3. The core mechanism appears to involve the enzyme Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including Calanphenanthrene A and Jasplakinolide Z1. These compounds are both predicted to interact with Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which in turn is predicted to target the pim-3 kinase. This indicates that Lambertiainc Acid may act as a modulator of Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, potentially influencing the activity of pim-3 through this intermediate. The evidence supports a mechanism where Lambertiainc Acid could either directly interact with pim-3 or indirectly regulate its activity via the Isoleucine--tRNA ligase pathway. The high scores in the paths suggest that the relationship is well-supported, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
